SUMMARY:Wheelhouse Wednesday
DESCRIPTION:Offshore Wind Drinks – Houston\nHosted By National Wildlife Federation – Free event. Please sign up to attend\nFor nearly twenty years\, Texas has led the nation in producing wind power. Texas now hosts nearly 20\,000 active wind turbines—more than the next three states (Iowa\, Oklahoma\, and California) combined! Offshore Wind presents a remarkable opportunity for Texas to continue its role as a maritime industry and energy leader. Enthusiastic support and advanced planning will ensure that Texas is ready to advance responsible offshore wind development in the years to come. \nThe National Wildlife Federation invites you to join us for Offshore Wind Drinks on Wednesday\, August 26th\, at 6 pm CDT\, at the Houston Maritime Center and Museum. \nThis event will feature guest speaker Janet Harreld\, the Executive Director of the Office of Continuing Education at the University of Houston-Downtown (UHD). \nJoin us to learn more about UHD’s Wind Turbine Technician Program and the ways that Texas is already contributing to the development of offshore wind energy on the East Coast. \nCome mix and mingle while learning about this emerging\, reliable energy option that is producing power and creating high-quality jobs. \nWe hope you’ll join us! \nSign Up Here https://www.mobilize.us/nwf/event/996730/
URL:https://houstonmaritime.org/event/wheelhouse-wednesday/
LOCATION:Houston Maritime Center & Museum\, 2940 Riverby Rd\, Suite 200\, Houston\, TX\, 77020\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://houstonmaritime.org/wp-content/uploads/OSW-Drinks-2026-Houston-940-x-788-px-2.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Houston Maritime Museum":MAILTO:info@houstonmaritime.org
END:VEVENT
